## First Tree Family

The generated Context Tree Policy is always present. Skills below load on
demand from their `description`; trust auto-injected routing for general
harness skills (`tdoc`, `review`, `simplify`, `update-config`, …).

| Skill | Load when |
|---|---|
| `first-tree-welcome` | the First Tree onboarding first chat — a natural welcome / "help me get started" message from the user; not a repo scan or tree setup chat, and never an external-channel or `type=integration` message such as Feishu, even when it is a new chat or greeting |
| `first-tree-read`    | read relevant Context Tree files before acting from task / path / feature signals |
| `first-tree-write`   | reflect a concrete source artifact (PR/MR, design doc, meeting note, review thread, or pasted source) into the Context Tree |
| `first-tree-seed`    | bootstrap the team's Context Tree from readable sources (declared repos or a local Git repo / GitHub or GitLab URL supplied in chat); create + bind if none exists, fill a bound-but-empty tree, or continue Phase 2 after Phase 1 merges |
| `first-tree-qa` | test, validate, reproduce, release-qualify, or assess performance by establishing the complete product harness before task-specific execution |
| `first-tree-file-bug` | you hit a bug in First Tree itself (CLI, runtime, chat, web, GitHub or GitLab integration, or tree tooling) and want it reported — gathers repro + version + chat/user IDs and opens an issue on First Tree's own repo (not the user's own/bound repo) via the user's `gh` CLI |
| `context-tree-review` | a trusted provider-scoped Context Reviewer run or an explicit request to review a GitHub Context Tree PR or GitLab MR; GitHub publishes an App verdict, while GitLab uses Reviewer-local notes, repair, push, and exact-SHA merge without the GitHub publisher |
| `context-tree-audit` | a human explicitly asks to audit the whole stored Context Tree, a domain, or selected normal paths for drift, contradictions, duplication, density, metadata, placement, or relationship problems |<% } else if (contextTree.source === 'local') { %>

